mulate american culture  they brought american culture back to  liberia their intentions were not to be  africans  libera's history does not start with the  arrival of african americans jones  believes some of the street names should  reference the nation's 17 indigenous  groups an effort to be made to preserve  the diverse architectural history of the  country as an increasing number of  african-americans make liberia their  home laura pritchard believes there's so  much to learn from the past  in order to build a better future for  all librarians  nicholas hawk al-jazeera providence  island liberia
 

